So, if **4 towels take 4 hours to dry**, that means **each towel individually takes 4 hours** to dry under those conditions.

Therefore, **20 towels** (assuming they’re all spread out with equal sun/air access) will **also take 4 hours** to dry.

> ✅ **Answer: 4 hours.**

*(Note: In real life, overcrowding *might* increase drying time—but the question says "exact same conditions", implying ideal, non-interfering setup.)*
